From 6923427ef75375bc1b17c04b8933abd0e4f00224 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 22:33:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1661/3799] soh: rename func_80086D5C ->
 Interface_ClearIntBuffer

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: zeroes a run of s32 values.
Defined in soh/src/code/z_parameter.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/z_parameter.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/z_parameter.c b/soh/src/code/z_parameter.c
index 77ad1b889..00d6464a4 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/z_parameter.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/z_parameter.c
@@ -2772,7 +2772,8 @@ bool Inventory_HatchPocketCucco(PlayState* play) {
     return 1;
 }
 
-void func_80086D5C(s32* buf, u16 size) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_80086D5C: zeroes a run of s32 values.
+void Interface_ClearIntBuffer(s32* buf, u16 size) {
     for (u16 i = 0; i < size; i++) {
         buf[i] = 0;
     }
-- 
